## 📌 Project Overview

This project is a personal implementation of a functional **HTTP/1.1 web server built directly on top of Python's low-level networking primitives**.

The server communicates with clients through raw TCP sockets, manually processes incoming HTTP requests, resolves requested resources from the filesystem, determines the appropriate MIME type, constructs HTTP responses, and transmits the resulting data back to the client.

The implementation deliberately avoids high-level web frameworks such as:

* Flask
* FastAPI
* Django
* Third-party HTTP libraries

The goal is to understand the fundamental mechanisms behind web servers and the relationship between:

```text
🌐 Client
   ↓
📡 HTTP/1.1
   ↓
🔌 TCP
   ↓
⚙️ OS Socket API
   ↓
📂 File System
   ↓
📨 HTTP Response
```

