# ⚙️ Getting Started

## 📋 Requirements

* Python 3.x
* A Unix-like operating system or Windows with Python installed.

No external dependencies are required.

---

## 1️⃣ Clone the Repository

```bash
git clone <repository-url>
cd custom-http-server
```

---

## 2️⃣ Start the Server

```bash
python servidor.py
```

The server will be available at:

```text
http://localhost:8080
```

---

## 3️⃣ Open the Application

Navigate to:

```text
http://localhost:8080
```

The server will serve resources from:

```text
public/
```

---

## 4️⃣ Stop the Server

Press:

```text
Ctrl + C
```

The server will handle the interruption and close its resources safely.

---

# 🧪 Example Request Flow

When a client requests:

```http
GET /index.html HTTP/1.1
```

The server performs:

```text
/index.html
     ↓
📂 public/index.html
     ↓
🔍 File existence check
     ↓
🧾 MIME type detection
     ↓
📖 Read file as bytes
     ↓
📨 Build HTTP response
     ↓
📡 Send through TCP
     ↓
🌐 Browser renders content
```

